From 5da032e91f9a7b952fb6acdb32ebf27a82351e30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite Dev <dev@auralite.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:57:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] U5 update

USB end-to-end + hardening close-out. --no-usb-uhci (machine_t.
cfg_no_uhci) omits the UHCI companion -- the test_usb_ehci.sh
EHCI-only machine shape (-device usb-ehci, no -usb); unit vector
ok uhci omitted (open-bus I/O, no halt handshake, EHCI intact).
Both sticks through the guest's MSC path with /usb info + a sector
read typed over the KBC (run /apps/filesize /usb/sector0.bin):
UHCI companion lane (AURALUSB 8 MiB) and EHCI high-speed lane
(AURALEHC 8 MiB), each x2 sequential byte-identical (tests 25->26
vectors). test_ahci_matrix.sh MATRIX_DETERMINISM=1 green with all
four pairs byte-identical; AHCI/fs receipt lines byte-identical to
the S5-era lane logs (vmdrv PCI scan grows the intended U4
companion entry -- documented). Frozen-kernel reproducibility:
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1791484814 banner + 92160-byte trimmed initrd
reconstruction. Measured: 8 MiB /usb/disk.img over the UHCI 64-byte
chunk path costs ~21G instr (3880/16384 sectors per 8G) -- media
correctness stays pinned by ok uhci td walk. Docs: USB_PLAN U5
closed (U0-U5 done), CHANGELOG U1-U5, ROADMAP ledger, STATUS.
